buttonmatrix: pass the label length to the draw descriptor

LVGL 9.5 truncates button-matrix labels: the draw descriptor is built with
text_local set but no text_length, so the renderer reads a length of zero.

Origin: 3cae8ca ("feat: add oxivgl-sys workspace crate, download LVGL at
build time"), which restored this patch when the vendored sys crate replaced
the external lvgl_rust_sys dependency.

--- a/src/widgets/buttonmatrix/lv_buttonmatrix.c
+++ b/src/widgets/buttonmatrix/lv_buttonmatrix.c
@@ -766,6 +766,7 @@
         /*Draw the text*/
         draw_label_dsc_act.text = txt;
         draw_label_dsc_act.text_local = true;
+        draw_label_dsc_act.text_length = (uint32_t)lv_strlen(txt);
         draw_label_dsc_act.base.id1 = btn_i;
         lv_draw_label(layer, &draw_label_dsc_act, &btn_area);
     }
